# Scan fixtures: <file> <status>. Each .vhd lists its expected units in
# "-- expect: <line> <kind> <name>" comments, including the unit that
# follows each tricky construct, so a misplaced unit end shows up.
# The basic forms (instantiation, bindings, generic/nested packages,
# contexts, physical types, subprogram forms, generates) are covered in
# tests/scan_test.c; these add cases it does not have.
#
# status: pass   - must match exactly
#         xfail  - KNOWN GAP, expected to fail; CI stays green. If it
#                  starts passing, the test fails (XPASS) so the mark is
#                  removed. The text after "xfail" names the gap.
attribute_spec_classes.vhd    xfail scan.c gap: same as attribute_spec_subprogram and attribute_spec_units (function/procedure/units entity classes); the other classes here (entity, architecture, signal, label, type, component, package) pass alone
attribute_spec_component.vhd  pass
attribute_spec_package.vhd    pass
attribute_spec_subprogram.vhd xfail scan.c gap: subprogram_body() treats "attribute a of f : function|procedure is <value>;" as a body unless <value> is a single name, so depth never returns to 0 and the next unit is missed
attribute_spec_units.vhd      xfail scan.c gap: opens_block() counts "units" in "attribute a of t : units is 1;" as a units block, so the next unit is missed
case_generate.vhd             pass
case_in_process.vhd           pass
if_generate.vhd               pass
